  33:     """Compute a grey result bar by adding teal bar heights and subtracting red bar heights.
  34: 
  35:     Input structure
  36:     - The grid has a dominant background and several bottom-aligned one-cell-wide vertical bars.
  37:     - Teal bars are positive operands; red bars are negative operands.
  38:     - The penultimate column is an empty result slot.
  39: 
  40:     Rule
  41:     - Keep every input bar unchanged.
  42:     - Compute result height = total teal bar height - total red bar height.
  43:     - Paint that many bottom cells of the penultimate column grey.
  44: 
  45:     Key insight
  46:     - The bars encode arithmetic by height, with color providing the sign.
  47:     """
  48:     g = np.asarray(grid, dtype=int)
  49:     height, width = g.shape
  50:     bg = get_bg(g)
  51:     bars = _operand_bars(g, bg)
  52: 
  53:     result_height = 0
  54:     for bar in bars:
  55:         if bar["color"] == Color.TEAL:
  56:             result_height += bar["height"]
  57:         else:
  58:             assert bar["color"] == Color.RED
  59:             result_height -= bar["height"]
  60: 
  61:     assert 0 < result_height <= height
  62:     assert width >= 2
  63:     result_col = width - 2
  64:     assert bool(np.all(g[:, result_col] == bg))
